17. TESTING WITH DIFFERENT USER PREFERENCES

The recommendation system was tested with multiple combinations of user preferences to verify that the filtering and ranking process works correctly.

The tests considered different combinations of:

• City
• Cuisine
• Price range
• Minimum rating
• Online delivery preference
• Number of recommendations

This testing verifies that the recommendation system is not dependent on one fixed user input.

18. RECOMMENDATION VALIDATION

The returned recommendations were checked against the selected user preferences.

The validation process verifies:

• The recommended restaurant belongs to the requested city.
• The recommended restaurant contains the requested cuisine.
• The restaurant satisfies the selected price range.
• The restaurant meets the minimum rating requirement.
• The restaurant satisfies the online delivery requirement when specified.

This provides a direct validation that the hard filtering constraints are respected.

19. HANDLING INVALID INPUTS

Input validation was added to improve the robustness of the recommendation function.

For example, the function checks that:

• City is not empty.
• Cuisine is not empty.
• Price range is between 1 and 4.
• Minimum rating is between 0 and 5.

Invalid values result in meaningful ValueError messages instead of unexpected behavior.

20. HANDLING NO-RESULT CASES

The system also handles situations where no restaurant satisfies all the selected preferences.

When no matching restaurant is found, the function displays an appropriate message and returns an empty DataFrame rather than producing an unexpected error.

This improves the usability and robustness of the recommendation system.

21. SIMILARITY ANALYSIS

The similarity score represents how closely the restaurant content matches the user's textual preferences.

Restaurants with higher similarity scores are more closely aligned with the requested cuisine and location information.

The similarity score represents content similarity and should not be interpreted as a probability that the user will like a particular restaurant.

22. RECOMMENDATION RESULT ANALYSIS

The final recommendations are ranked using the Final Score, which combines content similarity and restaurant rating.

A restaurant can achieve a high position in the recommendation list when it has strong alignment with the requested preferences and a relatively high rating.

The final ranking therefore considers both preference matching and restaurant quality as represented by the available rating information.

