24. RESULTS

The task successfully implemented a content-based restaurant recommendation system.

The complete workflow includes:

• Restaurant data preparation
• Text normalization
• User preference handling
• Input validation
• Preference-based filtering
• TF-IDF vectorization
• Cosine similarity calculation
• Rating score normalization
• Final ranking score calculation
• Top N recommendation generation
• Recommendation validation
• No-result handling
• Multiple preference testing

The resulting system can generate restaurant recommendations dynamically according to the user's selected preferences.

25. KEY FINDINGS

The recommendation system demonstrates that restaurant attributes can be used to build an explainable content-based recommendation approach.

Cuisine and location-related information provide the primary basis for similarity matching, while price range, minimum rating, and online delivery are used as explicit filtering constraints.

Combining similarity with normalized restaurant rating allows the ranking to consider both preference alignment and restaurant rating.

The implementation also demonstrates that input validation and no-result handling can improve the reliability of a recommendation system.

26. LIMITATIONS

• The dataset does not contain historical user-restaurant interaction data such as clicks, bookings, purchases, or personalized feedback.
• Standard personalized recommendation metrics such as precision@K, recall@K, or NDCG cannot be reliably calculated without suitable user interaction or relevance data.
• The content similarity depends on the textual information available in the dataset.
• Price range, minimum rating, and online delivery are primarily used as filtering constraints rather than being fully represented within the TF-IDF similarity calculation.
• The 0.7 similarity and 0.3 rating weights are manually selected design parameters.
• The system recommends restaurants based on the available dataset attributes and does not guarantee actual user satisfaction.
• A content-based system may provide limited personalization because it does not learn from individual user history.

27. CONCLUSION

A content-based restaurant recommendation system was successfully developed using the restaurant dataset provided for the Cognifyz Technologies Machine Learning Internship.

The system accepts user preferences including city, cuisine, price range, minimum rating, and online delivery. Restaurants are first filtered according to these constraints and then ranked using TF-IDF-based cosine similarity.

A normalized rating score is combined with the similarity score using the formula:

Final Score = 0.7 × Similarity Score + 0.3 × Rating Score

The resulting restaurants are sorted according to their Final Score and the Top N recommendations are returned.

The recommendation function also includes input validation and no-result handling, making the system more robust for different user inputs.

Multiple preference scenarios were used to test the system and validate that the recommendations satisfy the specified constraints.

Overall, this task provided practical experience in content-based recommendation systems, text preprocessing, TF-IDF, cosine similarity, preference-based filtering, ranking, input validation, testing, and interpretation of recommendation-system limitations.

